{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity","id":1002012,"title":"A Possibility....Supernautral Solidarity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-11T17:56:33-08:00","id":1002012,"title":"A Possibility....Supernautral Solidarity","content":"Although I'm aware that by default, supernaturals either stay away from each other or kill each on sight due to their own reasons but here's a another interesting proposal which would especially fit into the Gothic Punk theme of the WoD.<br /> <br /> What about a scenario with all All Types of Supernaturals stand in solidarity and co-exist with each other especially the &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; of what's going on which would mirror the intersectional feminist/leftist settlements.<br /> <br /> Or rather picture this, a Kindred, a Garou or other Shapeshifter, a Mage, Demon, Fae/Changeling, Risen, etc all in the same team/group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T18:25:00-08:00","id":1002027,"title":"","content":"What could threaten all of them enough to make them play nice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:50:16-08:00","id":1002060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity#post1002012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...which would mirror the intersectional feminist/leftist settlements...</div> </div> </div> </div>I... <u><b>really</b></u> didn't get what you meant with this.<br /> <br /> That said, there are a lot of options, depending on how far you're disposed to drift from default WoD. If you want to dissociate too much, I can suggest that you look for CoD, that can far more easily support this kind of play.<br /> <br /> But we do have a lot of options in the WoD (somewhat)properly. I did it a lot of times, indeed, and always figured up the End Times as a moment for such solidarity to avoid common destruction under the various annihilation forces coming. I thought of it, indeed, since the 90s, on my very beginning with the setting.<br /> <br /> We can have such group, first, by dint of individuality. As staple to the setting as the enmity among the supernaturals is their relationships. Relationships between Kindred and Garou are common enough to be both a Merit for both since there are Merits, and a common cautionary tale among both species. It is such a hated thing because it is a thing to begin with. Similar tales, if less common, can be found about any other combination you can imagine. In short, such a group can form simply because the characters involved are driven, by destiny, personal qualities or circumstances, to gather and cooperate. The cost they will pay is the necessity of balancing this with their obligations with their respective societies. Unsurprisingly, such things are more common among castaways and exiled members of those societies.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there <u>are</u> instances of cooperation that can play a role. Werewolves are suspicious of Mages, but not instant-enemies (this is just with Vampires). They have a history with the Fae, specially the Fianna, and with the sources of the Risen, specially the Silent Striders. Changellings are actually known to <u>look for</u> other supernaturals, it isn't at all strange or uncommon from their perspective. Vampires tend to be pretty paranoid, but they're also used to deal with people even at that, They are, after all, social and paranoid among themselves as a rule of thumb. Mages and Risen have nothing at all by default against anyone. With Mages being driven by Paradigm, hubris and curiosity, and the Risen having their own purpose and goals, they are certainly cautious of others and others should be cautious about them, but nothing here is default.<br /> <br /> Demons are a special case in any case. Their current status is very new, while their previous history made them the default enemy of anyone, to an extreme not seem anywhere. To put them in this is a little tricky.<br /> <br /> For now I won't talk about any given way of altering the setting to make this more common, but another thing have to be evaluated. Crossovers have too strong an influence on the themes of the game. That's the main reason it isn't used too much. Each splat have its own themes. In a crossover, those themes are heavily weakened by the others, while new themes arise. And few people have a good grasp of how this works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:01:28-08:00","id":1002063,"title":"","content":"Every facet of their existence would bring them into conflict, constantly. There can be no cohesion when vampires are a problem that Garou and Fera deal with when they have them time, to name but one example issue. You'd have to completely rewrite the most important details of each splat to make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:04:30-08:00","id":1002064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002060#post1002060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Werewolves are suspicious of Mages, but not instant-enemies (this is just with Vampires)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are caern robbers and the central pillar of their game is a complete inversion of everything in Werewolf. They would be a hair's-breadth away from starting a fight to the death, constantly, because mages just don't understand the concept of &quot;hands off this, you don't get to eat it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:36:05-08:00","id":1002071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002064#post1002064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are caern robbers and the central pillar of their game is a complete inversion of everything in Werewolf. They would be a hair's-breadth away from starting a fight to the death, constantly, because mages just don't understand the concept of &quot;hands off this, you don't get to eat it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> On a default level, it is true. Mages have their own beliefs and a general penchant for considering their own knowledge superior, their own necessities more important, and any discord as born of obvious ignorance from the other side. They need nodes, and since Caerns work as nodes, they get them. Vampires are commonly thought as servants of the Wyrm and creations of the Wyrm, things the average werewolf don't bother to distinguish.<br /> <br /> But it is just a default, in a world of idiosyncrasies.<br /> <br /> A vampire doesn't have at all to serve the Wyrm, or to &quot;reek&quot; of it. Most never even heard of it, and high-humanity Vampires usually don't click as Wyrm-Tainted (the common benchmark is Humanity 7 or above). A Mage is defined by Paradigm and individual perspective. A lot of Mages follow very well the concept of hands-off. What you describes is mostly valid for Hermetics, and in minor degree for Technomancers and Technocrats. By the way, there are described alliances between the Fera and the Dreamspeakers, just for the most common. No Mage is at a compulsion to steal nodes and ignore advice as if it was their frenzy.<br /> <br /> No important aspect have to be rewritten, either. Just link vampires to the Weaver instead of the Wyrm from the Garou/Fera perspective and you can get rid of their enmity without changing any other aspect of the games. You don't need even this for Mages, just make them know more about werewolves and the reverse also true.<br /> <br /> You see, I'm not saying it isn't valid to play those games as irreconcilable. But it isn't in the games to such a degree. What it seems is more that you got the default vision of the Garou over the other two splats and assumed it as inherent and unavoidable truth. It isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:14:06-08:00","id":1002100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002071#post1002071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree.<br /> <br /> On a default level, it is true. Mages have their own beliefs and a general penchant for considering their own knowledge superior, their own necessities more important, and any discord as born of obvious ignorance from the other side. They need nodes, and since Caerns work as nodes, they get them. Vampires are commonly thought as servants of the Wyrm and creations of the Wyrm, things the average werewolf don't bother to distinguish.</div> </div> </div> </div>And mages have an effect on the world not unlike nexus crawlers or possibly dream banes (it's difficult to tell when one critical charm that they would use to accomplish this hasn't been detailed, ever). It really shouldn't be cordial as it's presented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it is just a default, in a world of idiosyncrasies.<br /> <br /> A vampire doesn't have at all to serve the Wyrm, or to &quot;reek&quot; of it. Most never even heard of it, and high-humanity Vampires usually don't click as Wyrm-Tainted (the common benchmark is Humanity 7 or above). A Mage is defined by Paradigm and individual perspective. A lot of Mages follow very well the concept of hands-off. What you describes is mostly valid for Hermetics, and in minor degree for Technomancers and Technocrats. By the way, there are described alliances between the Fera and the Dreamspeakers, just for the most common. </div> </div> </div>How many Mage paradigms are going to be alright with the Impergium? Even the Dreamspeakers probably wouldn't want to be anywhere near that hot potato. Even if they think that was wrong, how about the Ratkin's reason for being? They're meant to keep human numbers very low, and this isn't an unfortunate flaw in the system, but a necessary action that they've not been able to take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No Mage is at a compulsion to steal nodes and ignore advice as if it was their frenzy. </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> <br /> Garou would tend to warn them that they would die if they came anywhere near it. Several &quot;curious&quot; mage dismemberings later, the mages would probably cut off ties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No important aspect have to be rewritten, either. Just link vampires to the Weaver instead of the Wyrm from the Garou/Fera perspective and you can get rid of their enmity without changing any other aspect of the games. </div> </div> </div>Pattern spiders and drones are not your friend, so no, that doesn't work. They're already noxious, unknowing Weaver-spawn as-is, so having them key even more off of the thing that bound the Wyrm (causing this mess in the first place) and is insanely obsessed with perfection and order is not a step up..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need even this for Mages, just make them know more about werewolves and the reverse also true. </div> </div> </div>If Garou knew more about mages, they probably would have found them worrying enough to kill off. Look at how the Fera weathered their close contact; the arc of the game's history is &quot;allies of the Garou tend to end up being killed by Garou&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You see, I'm not saying it isn't valid to play those games as irreconcilable. But it isn't in the games to such a degree. What it seems is more that you got the default vision of the Garou over the other two splats and assumed it as inherent and unavoidable truth. It isn't. </div> </div> </div>Mage and Werewolf are inherently irreconcilable due to taking opposite extreme viewpoints on the world down to the tiniest cosmological detail. Also, Mage has an irreconcilable differences of cosmology with every other game, in its interpretation of what makes the world work and what technology is. That's what comes of trying to put way, way too much of Ars Magica in a setting that was its own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:42:38-08:00","id":1002109,"title":"","content":"Well, there can only be one foundation of reality, though no one has to be particularly close to it (H.P. Lovecraft assumed that the foundation of reality could never be understood by human minds and could only be approximated by civilizations that were ancient when the first insects crawled from the seas of the Earth). As for cooperation, there are going to be factions within each race that will not play nice with others. The Sabbat of the Kindred, the Black Spiral Dancers and (for completely different reasons) the Red Talons of the Garou, the Scorpion Eaters of the Kuei-jin, the Technocracy, etc would refuse to join forces with other groups of supernaturals. <br /> <br /> The best bet would be Asia. You might be able to ally the Beast Courts, Hsien, and Kuei-jin Courts against the Demon Emperor (and they might have a chance). Outside of the borders of Asia, I cannot think of anything that would bring together the Camarilla, the Fera, and the Kithain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:58:17-08:00","id":1002216,"title":"","content":"Post Apocalyptic setting:<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Antediluvians have awoken. They're eating... everything. Fae, Mages, Shifters... anything with Power. A group of PCs there can be just about anything that wants to live. (Say using a sextant to chart the movements of Lasombra's anti-Sun dark disk in the sky to keep ahead of him in the Americas, while a Rank 6 Simba with ties to Ra and powers of the Sun forges an Alliance with the Amenti to hold onto a chunk of Africa. as the children of Malkav throw themselves at them like Celtic Berserkers.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T08:01:06-08:00","id":1002220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002100#post1002100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And mages have an effect on the world not unlike nexus crawlers or possibly dream banes (it's difficult to tell when one critical charm that they would use to accomplish this hasn't been detailed, ever). It really shouldn't be cordial as it's presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Nexus Crawlers leave the threads of the Tellurian in tatters, and have no control or reason at all. And werewolves so completely understand by instinct what Awakened Magic does that they certainly see things that way when they look at a gal that most of the time just seems lucky, and at the rest of the time have reasonably understandable and educated (if maybe unbelievable) explanations for whatever she does, since Paradigm is a system to your magic. If you were talking about Nefandi, it would be true, for sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002100#post1002100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Mage paradigms are going to be alright with the Impergium? Even the Dreamspeakers probably wouldn't want to be anywhere near that hot potato. Even if they think that was wrong, how about the Ratkin's reason for being? They're meant to keep human numbers very low, and this isn't an unfortunate flaw in the system, but a necessary action that they've not been able to take.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you assume the Impergium as population control, a lot of them, actually. Among the Verbena it would be particularly popular. If you assume it as the extinction of humanity, certainly very few. If you assume it as just acceptable history, them even more Mages, except for the ones who will think you a coward for not going further to population control, and the madman that want humanity's end.<br /> <br /> Now, how many <u>werewolves</u> are alright with the Impergium nowadays, again?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002100#post1002100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou would tend to warn them that they would die if they came anywhere near it. Several &quot;curious&quot; mage dismemberings later, the mages would probably cut off ties.</div> </div> </div> </div>You simply ignored what I said. That's fine, so I'll say it again. As there are Garou and Garou, there are Mages and Mages. And a lot of Mages would heed the advice and keep away. They would look out for their own holly places and try to earn the right for being at a Caern without pushing the matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002100#post1002100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern spiders and drones are not your friend, so no, that doesn't work. They're already noxious, unknowing Weaver-spawn as-is, so having them key even more off of the thing that bound the Wyrm (causing this mess in the first place) and is insanely obsessed with perfection and order is not a step up..</div> </div> </div> </div>Pattern-Spiders and Drones are just one aspect of the Weaver, and a lot of werewolves are willing at least to some extend to deal with the Weaver. Specially with things that are just touched by it, not fighting for it. And again, there are Vampires and Vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002100#post1002100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Garou knew more about mages, they probably would have found them worrying enough to kill off. Look at how the Fera weathered their close contact; the arc of the game's history is &quot;allies of the Garou tend to end up being killed by Garou&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, it doesn't work that way for every single Garou in the world. And there are Mages with paradigm close enough to want to work with werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002100#post1002100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage and Werewolf are inherently irreconcilable due to taking opposite extreme viewpoints on the world down to the tiniest cosmological detail. Also, Mage has an irreconcilable differences of cosmology with every other game, in its interpretation of what makes the world work and what technology is. That's what comes of trying to put way, way too much of Ars Magica in a setting that was its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That have absolutely nothing to do with alliances. If any side were so obsessive with worldview to not accept allies with &quot;irreconcilable cosmological viewpoints&quot;, there wouldn't exist neither a Counsel of Nine Traditions, nor a Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I won't talk this further, its derailing the thread. The OP said he was aware of the difficulties. I said they don't have to exist in an individual level. You made it already clear that you don't think it possible in the canon, but it isn't the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002109#post1002109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there can only be one foundation of reality, though no one has to be particularly close to it (H.P. Lovecraft assumed that the foundation of reality could never be understood by human minds and could only be approximated by civilizations that were ancient when the first insects crawled from the seas of the Earth). As for cooperation, there are going to be factions within each race that will not play nice with others. The Sabbat of the Kindred, the Black Spiral Dancers and (for completely different reasons) the Red Talons of the Garou, the Scorpion Eaters of the Kuei-jin, the Technocracy, etc would refuse to join forces with other groups of supernaturals.<br /> <br /> The best bet would be Asia. You might be able to ally the Beast Courts, Hsien, and Kuei-jin Courts against the Demon Emperor (and they might have a chance). Outside of the borders of Asia, I cannot think of anything that would bring together the Camarilla, the Fera, and the Kithain.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the North Africa there was a great alliance once, and it didn't ended in bickering, just in growing isolation for each side. This alliance remains in the collective memory as the Egyptian mythology. Isis was a Mage, Osiris was a Vampire, Anubis was a Garou, Sobek was a Mokol\u00e9 turned Abomination by Set (it's still &quot;alive&quot;, though torpid), among others, and they are the very origin of the Mummies. So I think it reasonably feasible for an alliance there.<br /> <br /> The Assamites and Salubri in the Middle East would be fairly more amicable to Garou and Magi than to other vampires, and share the general goal of saving the world instead of saving their own skins. Even more they would ally to the Ahl'I'Batin after conversion to Islam.<br /> <br /> On Africa survival is usually a more pressing matter. The Fera of the continent are forming the Ahadi, similar to the Emerald Courts but with far less rigid structure, and their inspiration is precisely the old egyptian alliance. African vampires are usually a problem, of course, but it isn't impossible for them to ally with less destructive Kindred.<br /> <br /> Canada already hold a tentative alliance between Garou and Camarilla in Vancouver, and it went fairly well for some time. Some shady events ended it and started a war between both factions, but as much as it shows how hard it is for them to ally, it also shows such alliance is possible. It truly happened, and it truly worked.<br /> <br /> By myself, I use alliance between members of distinct factions frequently, and it never posed so much of a problem (usually it is secret, of course), nor did I felt my WoD less WoDish for doing that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002216#post1002216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post Apocalyptic setting:<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Antediluvians have awoken. They're eating... everything. Fae, Mages, Shifters... anything with Power. A group of PCs there can be just about anything that wants to live. (Say using a sextant to chart the movements of Lasombra's anti-Sun dark disk in the sky to keep ahead of him in the Americas, while a Rank 6 Simba with ties to Ra and powers of the Sun forges an Alliance with the Amenti to hold onto a chunk of Africa. as the children of Malkav throw themselves at them like Celtic Berserkers.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems rather fun. But we could make it with other Times of Judgement. I'm building some ideas, already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T10:37:30-08:00","id":1002262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002100#post1002100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage and Werewolf are inherently irreconcilable due to taking opposite extreme viewpoints on the world down to the tiniest cosmological detail. Also, Mage has an irreconcilable differences of cosmology with every other game, in its interpretation of what makes the world work and what technology is. That's what comes of trying to put way, way too much of Ars Magica in a setting that was its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't the Black Furies allied to the Verbenae and Dreamspeakers though? I don't think they necessarily need to be so terribly antagonistic in essence when there are presented cases things go just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T10:38:59-08:00","id":1002264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002262#post1002262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't the Black Furies allied to the Verbenae and Dreamspeakers though?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to depend on the writer/edition. And &quot;allied&quot; is a strong term besides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:56:50-08:00","id":1002291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002262#post1002262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't the Black Furies allied to the Verbenae and Dreamspeakers though? I don't think they necessarily need to be so terribly antagonistic in essence when there are presented cases things go just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less 'allied' and more 'not actively hostile'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:08:22-08:00","id":1004617,"title":"","content":"I think it would be very possible to change the setting into something like that of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Watch_(2004_film)\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Night Watch</i></a> movies, where various sorts of supernaturals interact and work together and cultural groups are based more on goals and geography than specific kind of creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T15:04:39-08:00","id":1004665,"title":"","content":"That would be a fairly major setting change and would require some better crossover rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T17:40:08-08:00","id":1004720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002109#post1002109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best bet would be Asia. You might be able to ally the Beast Courts, Hsien, and Kuei-jin Courts against the Demon Emperor (and they might have a chance). Outside of the borders of Asia, I cannot think of anything that would bring together the Camarilla, the Fera, and the Kithain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alien invasion, X-Com style","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T17:48:22-08:00","id":1004723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1002027#post1002027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could threaten all of them enough to make them play nice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nephandi...<br /> <br /> Also, it always stroke me odd when people vehemently argued against any kind of crossover, or different splats working together, because of &quot;antagonistic worldviews&quot;. In my book, vampire, werewolves, mages, changelings, all of them are persons and they living in not isolated, but more or less autonomous communities, so they could have their own reasons for working together, even vampires and werewolves sometimes.<br /> <br /> Not everyone is a total religious fanatic, not even the weres and I think the &quot;shoot on sight, or warn once then shoot&quot; is a way too exaggerated attitude and assumes that everyone in every splat's every community are toeing that party line every time. I'm not saying the game doesn't have space for that, but it also has space for more nuanced approaches. Note that it's still far from clapping hands and singing kumbaya together.<br /> <br /> For example I liked how the situation turned out in the Penny Dreadful novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-17-2016, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T18:49:02-08:00","id":1004744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1004723#post1004723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nephandi...<br /> <br /> Also, it always stroke me odd when people vehemently argued against any kind of crossover, or different splats working together, because of &quot;antagonistic worldviews&quot;. In my book, vampire, werewolves, mages, changelings, all of them are persons and they living in not isolated, but more or less autonomous communities, so they could have their own reasons for working together, even vampires and werewolves sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I argue against it for metatextual reasons, namely that the themes of each line tend to get up in each others' faces. Especially Mage, speak of the devil-worshippers; there's no compelling reason that their antagonists should be so important that all of the other monsters (if you can even call Mages monsters; if you wanted to have witches or the like as a splats, some kith of changeling would have done better) give even one iota of support to them, or need to. Hence why I insist that you would have to completely root up all of the assumptions of the world and start from scratch, Simple rearrangements will not cut it, because the games were made to collapse completely on contact with each other (yes, even with all of the crossover that existed in earlier editions; how much can you take in one go, and how much do you have to throw out in order to play?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not everyone is a total religious fanatic, not even the weres and I think the &quot;shoot on sight, or warn once then shoot&quot; </div> </div> </div>Very few Garou and Fera are religious, as such. Every worry and evil in their world view is very real and very dangerous, and doesn't rely on any belief or lack thereof to cause problems. That, in turn, is why they take a dim view of the groups that I mentioned earlier in the thread - they can regularly see all of the spiritual threats that swirl around vampires, and mages just don't understand, so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is a way too exaggerated attitude and assumes that everyone in every splat's every community are toeing that party line every time. I'm not saying the game doesn't have space for that, but it also has space for more nuanced approaches. Note that it's still far from clapping hands and singing kumbaya together. </div> </div> </div>You see banes brewing around vampires and their victims, you're going to decide on your own something is amiss with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example I liked how the situation turned out in the Penny Dreadful novel. </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer to forget that such a thing exists. But then, it is Mage, and I am who I am.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:22:32-08:00","id":1004781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1004744#post1004744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I argue against it for metatextual reasons, namely that the themes of each line tend to get up in each others' faces.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very much speaking in absolutes. All the games have their own unique themes, but I think there could be enough overlap between the lines and a crossover could bring in even new themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially Mage, speak of the devil-worshippers; there's no compelling reason that their antagonists should be so important that all of the other monsters (if you can even call Mages monsters; if you wanted to have witches or the like as a splats, some kith of changeling would have done better) give even one iota of support to them, or need to. </div> </div> </div>1. Nephandi aren't devil-worshippers. 2. It was just an example. The Pentex, Sabbat, Earthbounds, or any other big bad could be the common enemy. Accidentally there's overlap right there, since there are connections between the Nephandi and Pentex. Nephandi is a particularly good common enemy, because they have their filthy fingers in basically every pie and insidious and also pure evil. But Pentex could be a problem for vampires, banes could be a problem for mages, technocracy could be a problem for garou, sabbat for changelings, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simple rearrangements will not cut it, because the games were made to collapse completely on contact with each other (yes, even with all of the crossover that existed in earlier editions; how much can you take in one go, and how much do you have to throw out in order to play?). </div> </div> </div>Again you state your opinion as hard facts, while a lot of groups around the world and through the years played enjoyable crossovers and even the books themselves and the fiction assumed a more-or-less crossovered world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Very few Garou and Fera are religious, as such. Every worry and evil in their world view is very real and very dangerous, and doesn't rely on any belief or lack thereof to cause problems. That, in turn, is why they take a dim view of the groups that I mentioned earlier in the thread - they can regularly see all of the spiritual threats that swirl around vampires, and mages just don't understand, so. </div> </div> </div>Someone, who acts against someone else based on what she is, not on what she does is a fanatic in my eyes. It's too easy to condemn. A threat is not an act. A vampire and a mage could do good or bad just as a garou. And I agree with the opinion that certain mages indeed could understand and relate to the garou's cause and problems, especially kinfolk mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You see banes brewing around vampires and their victims, you're going to decide on your own something is amiss with them. </div> </div> </div>You see banes brewing around people who causes misery around them, it's not a vampire privilege. Trends are still not absolutes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd prefer to forget that such a thing exists. But then, it is Mage, and I am who I am. </div> </div> </div>Indeed and that's fine! Different tastes and all that. I liked it pretty much. We don't have to agree. Just please don't state your personal opinion and preferred approach as hard fact when it contradicts even with the books and canonical fiction. There are rules for crossover in the books, thus crossover is a supported, if not the default approach. There are strong crossover elements in the various games' metaplots and setting right there in the corebooks and there are plenty of crossover stories in the fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T02:43:58-08:00","id":1004851,"title":"","content":"Solidarity is less likely to grow out of current structures rather than the edges of various societies pushing together to form a new whole. That is to say the Camarilla is unlikely to be making new ground with other groups, they are entrenched in the current power structure but Anarchs and other dispossessed kindred are more likely to shake up the status quo as they have little hold in it.<br /> <br /> That being said the other groups don't have an easy coalition partner for said anarchs except Wraiths and Anarchs generally have little access to Necromancy to make such things work. Our next best group to work with them might be various Fae groups because they have class struggle written to an epic degree, on the other hand kindred are considered to be particularly banal and the need to hold onto humanity/path is in the end a drive towards stability that is at odds with the Kithain condition.<br /> <br /> On Kindred and KJ, this happens. Bamboo princes and Anarchs do ally. OF course in a timeline where the GLO happens that well gets poisoned by the meme &quot;All KJ hate white people&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sabbat are so deeply on the side of &quot;NOoooooo&quot; for anything not trying to be alien monster so really only have much options with the KJ.<br /> <br /> Fera have a distinct issue with cultural flexability for all their claims of connection to the wyld they are beholden to cultures and traditions more stagnant and ancient than even Kindred society. But where as that is purely a cultural thing for Kindred a Fera's supernatural power is beholden to following their traditions making it very difficult to go off and make a functional different method for serving Gaia. There is of course the Wyrm as an alternative but that obviously has itsown issues. However the Fera do seem to have a level of potential soldiarity with Kithain but even there the issue is strained.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now we get to Mages. Mages where everyone is the revolutionary and the man keeping people down! Now on the surface presumably the Camarilla and Technocracy would make good Allies. They both want to hide the truth from people. They both value stability and have a vested intererst in the current power structure. On the other hand the Camarilla is the single greatest criminal conspiracy that the Technocracy does not control run by monsters who eat people and twist the powerful's minds. And teh Technocracy is a bunch of dangerous mortals with the power to destroy an Antedeluvian! So obviously there are issues. This before dealing with issues like the Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Traditions and the Disparate Alliance have similar issues being torn between holding onto traditional methods for power and becoming increasing marginalzied by the march of the Technocracy. However they are the push for adaptation and are very much for all their personal power on the Outs with power and could really use a game changer. Greater alliances with other supernaturals would broadly be beneficial as long as Mage sophestry is kept in check.. which is always the issue.<br /> <br /> Wraiths generally do seem to work with whoever they can deal with, but have the limits of the Shroud. On the other hand this often highly abusive on the side of Vampires and potentially so for Mages. Kithain generally don't have such issues generally lacking the power to compell the dead.<br /> <br /> Changelings are dependent upon natural wells of glamour and human creativity. This means they can share/compete with Mages, Fera, KJ for some potential sites(whether all freeholds caerns Nodes dragonests etc.are the same thing is an argument in and of itself but for this post I'm going to assume there are some places taht quality for all and some that are creature specific), They are also particularly fragile to broad based social engineering and need a level of chaos in their lives so they gain distinct advantages from alliances with Kindred and Mages. On the other hand as basically sapient living stories bound in human flesh their actions view of others are shaped by such.<br /> <br /> Demons that well has been poisoned by thousands of years of Infernalism. It would be increadibly difficult to prove &quot;I'm totally a good demon now make this pact with me..&quot; on the other hand if they could you get distinct advantages all around, but since most supernatural socieites have had to deal with thousands of years of infernalism welll...<br /> <br /> Hunters are individuals they don't really have groups to make an interaction with.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said there are broadly a number of canonical interactions on nonviolent fashions between various groups. The largest is the the SE asian model where broadly speaking local supernaturals will have some level of diplomatic ties with other supernaturals, while they may not be forming Wu/pack/cabals or chantrycourts they at least know who to talk to in various areas and have some level of diplomacy. This has the advantages of having a level of diplomacy, it also comes with a a distinct disadvantage. Familiarity means that they can plan for more extensive conflicts and the various sides don't have the advantages of being an unknown quality to each other, this has been used on a number of occasions by various sides.<br /> <br /> There are also of course groups that do contain multiple types. the True Hand, Clan/Family Giovanni, creating a group outside the current structures that has itsown method that might contain multiple groups would not be a stretch though it would of course be something small and out of the way.<br /> <br /> Another point one might wish to consider on how easy supernatural populations avoid eachother is the praticalities of enviroment. Most of what we consider the &quot;West&quot; in the WOD is written up with the USA as the standard which generally has signficantly lower population densities than Asia or Europe allowing for things to be more spread out and more likely to be the only game in town where resources are not as competative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:42:39-08:00","id":1004930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1004851#post1004851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fera have a distinct issue with cultural flexability for all their claims of connection to the wyld</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't actually claim to have that many solid connections to it, as the Wyld is dangerous and unhinged but necessary... as long as it's not too close to caerns. The Rite of Abcission, which breaks off and removes Wyld Thresholds from caerns, exists and is a thing, and the Black Furies are the ones who keep said rite. The ban on letting anything threaten a caern is<br /> <br /> Also, Fera is what Garou call the other changers. The only one with a connection to the Wyld is the Ratkin, and it wasn't wholly intentional or wanted. But oh boy do they revel in extreme, violent change at any opportunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they are beholden to cultures and traditions more stagnant and ancient than even Kindred society. But where as that is purely a cultural thing for Kindred a Fera's supernatural power is beholden to following their traditions making it very difficult to go off and make a functional different method for serving Gaia. </div> </div> </div>Less stagnant, because the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers do exist and are actually accepted, and their technology-related Gifts leave the one path that the Tremere have for the same purpose in the dust, while driving backward. Possibly also not that much more old, since the current society for the Garou at least is a result of a later convening, and was different back in earlier prehistory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is of course the Wyrm as an alternative but that obviously has itsown issues. However the Fera do seem to have a level of potential soldiarity with Kithain but even there the issue is strained. </div> </div> </div>It depends on whether or not you go with Changeling or Werewolf for lore. Oddly enough, they're more cooperative or willing to lend a hand in the latter, as the former claimed that sidhe had used some Fenrir as steeds for centuries, but you'll never find that tidbit in any Werewolf book ever written. Only that fae are incredibly diverting and were making the Fianna's tribal leader go a bit loopy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:26:03-08:00","id":1005012,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla would probably be the obvious nexus for the development of a solidarity alliance in the West. They have the most powerful individual actors and, quite frankly, they are built around the principle of doing what is needed for survival. They are also deeply invested in mortal society and would probably be willing to work with anyone who could preserve some of their investments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:06:44-08:00","id":1005124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1004930#post1004930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't actually claim to have that many solid connections to it, as the Wyld is dangerous and unhinged but necessary... as long as it's not too close to caerns. The Rite of Abcission, which breaks off and removes Wyld Thresholds from caerns, exists and is a thing, and the Black Furies are the ones who keep said rite. The ban on letting anything threaten a caern is<br /> <br /> Also, Fera is what Garou call the other changers. The only one with a connection to the Wyld is the Ratkin, and it wasn't wholly intentional or wanted. But oh boy do they revel in extreme, violent change at any opportunity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Less stagnant, because the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers do exist and are actually accepted, and their technology-related Gifts leave the one path that the Tremere have for the same purpose in the dust, while driving backward. Possibly also not that much more old, since the current society for the Garou at least is a result of a later convening, and was different back in earlier prehistory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Various Changing breeds including the Garou are beholden to a Renown System and litany that is older than human history. Even the most out of the box thinking is limited by the nature of renown and the granting of Gifts. Unlike Kindred who aren't say beholden to the Traditions of Caine to gain more Disciplines rather they can practice and develop things on theirown..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It depends on whether or not you go with Changeling or Werewolf for lore. Oddly enough, they're more cooperative or willing to lend a hand in the latter, as the former claimed that sidhe had used some Fenrir as steeds for centuries, but you'll never find that tidbit in any Werewolf book ever written. Only that fae are incredibly diverting and were making the Fianna's tribal leader go a bit loopy. </div> </div> </div>I am more coming at it from a pragmatic direction. Whether or not Sidhe rode Fenrir as steeds isn't really important to the modern day since no one's really bringing that up. Fae in general can benefit from the effects various changers bring to an area, on the other hand they may potentially be competing for Caerns which is an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T13:35:47-08:00","id":1005459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002012-a-possibility-supernautral-solidarity?p=1005124#post1005124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Various Changing breeds including the Garou are beholden to a Renown System and litany that is older than human history. Even the most out of the box thinking is limited by the nature of renown and the granting of Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate this kind of thinking. You are assuming that the circumstances under which the old rules were constructed have changed; this is not the case. The past justifications for Garou tradition are still valid going forward into the modern era. Those that disregard the Litany or the guidance of the spirits are not wiser for it.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers claim similar things, that casting off the hide-bound laws will grant freedom. Within the context of WtA, they are wrong... they are just replacing the authority of the Mother with something far, far worse.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-19-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}